          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.095,
            0.591,
            0.119
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.132,
            0.824,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": "We analysed some situations, asked questions, and found answers by first guessing, then modelling the problem statement, followed by making assumptions and approximations to carry out the calculations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.217,
            0.823,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": "We experienced how rapid exponential growth, also called multiplicative growth, can be compared to additive growth."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.27,
            0.821,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": "$n ^ { a }$ is $n \\times n \\times n \\times n \\times \\ldots \\times n$ (n multiplied by itself a times) and $n ^ { - a }   =   \\frac { 1 } { n ^ { a } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.302,
            0.546,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": " Operations with exponents satisfy"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.331,
            0.379,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "y $n ^ { a } \\times n ^ { b } = n ^ { a + b }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.354,
            0.427,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "\\bullet ( n ^ { a } ) ^ { b } = ( n ^ { b } ) ^ { a } = n ^ { a   \\times   b }",
          "image_source": "images/page_27_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.379,
            0.448,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "\\bullet \\; n^{a} \\div n^{b} = n^{a - b} \\; (n \\neq 0)",
          "image_source": "images/page_27_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.404,
            0.424,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "\\bullet \\; n^{a} \\times m^{a} = (n \\times m)^{a}",
          "image_source": "images/page_27_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.429,
            0.493,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "\\bullet \\; n^{a} \\div m^{a} = (n \\div m)^{a}(m \\neq 0)",
          "image_source": "images/page_27_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.452,
            0.381,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": "y $n ^ { 0 } = 1 \\; ( n \\neq 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.476,
            0.823,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "The scientific notation for the number 308100000 is $3 . 0 8 1 \\times 1 0 ^ { 8 } .$ The standard form of the scientific notation of any number is $x \\times 1 0 ^ { y } ,$ , where $x \\geq 1$ and $x < 1 0$ and y is an integer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.543,
            0.823,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "Engaging in interesting thought experiments can be used as means to understand how large a number or a quantity is."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
